<title>USA: LITTLE CHANGE SEEN IN BRAZIL COFFEE WEATHER - WSC.</title>
<headline>LITTLE CHANGE SEEN IN BRAZIL COFFEE WEATHER - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>No damaging cold is in sight for the coffee-growing areas of Brazil for the next five days, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Thursday.</p>
<p>There is a chance of a few light showers in the south today and Friday, but otherwise it will be mostly dry. Low temperatures will be 50-64 F.</p>
<p>Little change is expected through early next week, WSC said.</p>
<p>East-central Brazil was mainly dry on Wednesday, with highs of 64-82 F and lows of 50-64.</p>
</text>
